{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army","id":857414,"title":"Werewolf Delirium vs Army","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-01T19:54:28-07:00","id":857414,"title":"Werewolf Delirium vs Army","content":"Are there any rules regarding the effect of Delirium when a single werewolf is faced by overwhelming odds? We're running a Dark Ages game with a few mixed splats and we have a werehyena. As far as I can tell any werewcreature could simply stand in a field against a mortal army and they'd all flee in terror. This seems game breaking to me. Are there any precedents for something like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","name":"Seph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:22:00-07:00","id":857431,"title":"","content":"Are you taking into account the different reactions people have to the Delirium? If you're faced with an army you'll have to contend with quite a few people frothing at the mouth as they try to tear you limb from limb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:36:57-07:00","id":857441,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'm not that familiar with Werewolf. I mainly play Vampire. But a friend of ours hates Vampires and we managed to work her in as a metis werewhyena. I know that according to a chart in Werewolf at WP4 the reaction is to go berserk and attack the werecreature. But according to that chart, that's only 15% of the population, so that could still send the majority of an army of say 100 fleeing in terror (Also doesn't make sense to me that after 4 WP a mortal can't do anything but flee until they hit 7 WP)<br /> <br /> Even taking into consideration WP 7-10 reactions that would send 71% of the army fleeing in terror.<br /> <br /> I'm of the opinion that when the mortals obviously have the numerical advantage (say 20-30:1) that the effects of Delirium are lessened. But like I said I'm not that familiar with werewolf and I don;t want to start swinging the nerf bat out of ignorance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","name":"Seph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:34:50-07:00","id":857479,"title":"","content":"29% of an army can still be pretty powerful. Also consider that the army might have<br /> <br /> Ghouls (rule em as delirium immune) True faith. <br /> Formori and other possessed humans that are amoungst the army. Evil spirits often follow soldiers for the death and destruction they cause. <br /> Also, it's the dark ages, maybe people might have, on average, one higher willpower, because their souls haven't been drained by modern life. This also might go to for the army, as they are trained for terrifying situations. Maybe that might make some more dead inside, but others might get tougher. <br /> <br /> <b>Furthermore, points in the occult knowledge can reduce the effect of delirium. It's the dark ages. Everyone's religious, and that counts as occult (sorta).</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:38:10-07:00","id":857483,"title":"","content":"I've always ruled the delirium isn't in effect in mass combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:47:16-07:00","id":857488,"title":"","content":"But it is and has to be so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:50:15-07:00","id":857492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857479#post857479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Furthermore, points in the occult knowledge can reduce the effect of delirium. It's the dark ages. Everyone's religious, and that counts as occult (sorta).</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The roll is Wits + Occult at difficulty 9, so there's actually a pretty high risk of botching.<br /> <br /> But if this is the Dark Ages, the army is going to have to contend with Gifts like King of Beasts, Iron-Can't-Bite, and anything that might alter the temperature or levels of precipitation. Water-logging an army and starving it before going in for the kill may not have visceral appeal, but it's pretty much childishly easy if you have an Ajaba with the rain-bringing Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T22:04:32-07:00","id":857497,"title":"","content":"The problem with werecreatures is that they're so strong it's strange to think that any other enemy can beat them, then they loose. If the white howlers really wanted to, they could have driven rome out with a single pack and not needed to have risked their leaving their home unprotected. In the modern setting they're far superior to most other supernatural races (exceptions being on the most extreme ends of power) so i sometimes wonder why they haven't cleaned the earth yet. The answer; I don't know. Maybe god/gaia just doesn't want werecreatures meddling with humans that much, and so punishes those that interfere on such a massive scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T22:06:39-07:00","id":857498,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't get too hung up on the letter of the law, err rules, or what level of Willpower creates what effect and the what percentage of the population it is. Make the reaction appropriate considering the circumstances. Most people won't be able to fight effectively, but an army likely already has a different character than the average population - people who have seen close combat, who have killed before and been injured, who believe that God is on their side. If the army has a diverse composition, it might make sense that the peasant levies are too scared to fight, but maybe the knights can work up their courage to do so, while a few men at arms flee while others hurl themselves at the enemy in a rage. The rules are there to help, not constrain, you. Make the reaction of the army what you think the reaction should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 04-02-2016, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T22:35:43-07:00","id":857515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857483#post857483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always ruled the delirium isn't in effect in mass combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the way you think. Though our were-hyena doesn't care for it too much. I'm surprised she hasn't jumped on here yet honestly.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just to clarify, the were-hyena player was not trying to delirium an entire army. I was just concerned after my initial reading of the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","user":"Seph","date":". 04-02-2016, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","name":"Seph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T22:44:37-07:00","id":857517,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you don't like Delirium, if it breaks your game, then absolutely don't use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T03:46:58-07:00","id":857610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857479#post857479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Furthermore, points in the occult knowledge can reduce the effect of delirium. It's the dark ages. Everyone's religious, and that counts as occult (sorta).</b></div> </div> </div> </div>... say what? Being religious has nothing to do with having Occult. Nor does being a superstitious peasant doesn't count as having occult. Having a single dot of Occult is a dedicated pursuit of the topic in all its myriad forms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T04:00:10-07:00","id":857611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army#post857414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any rules regarding the effect of Delirium when a single werewolf is faced by overwhelming odds? We're running a Dark Ages game with a few mixed splats and we have a werehyena. As far as I can tell any werewcreature could simply stand in a field against a mortal army and they'd all flee in terror. This seems game breaking to me. Are there any precedents for something like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing to keep in mind that a uniform group of soldiers is not likely to have the same random willpower as the populace. There is a certain kind of people who end up in the military and those people are usually not the high willpower people. High Willpower people are extraordinary, I mean, look at this.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://imgur.com/IpcEgAM.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> And, define what does it mean to &quot;see&quot; a Werewolf in Crinos. If you're talking about a medieval army you're talking about the shifter being quite near them. The horror kicks in only after they actually realise what it is they are facing. As long as a Werewolf is at least 30-40 meters away, they will surely just think it's some big madman wearing wolfskins. Once he gets closer he will start provoking the delirum, but before that he might easily get peppered with arrows or a cunning commander may try to fall back to protect his men.<br /> <br /> However, once he's among them or clearly visible... they are fucked. Truly and utterly. Not only is a horrible death dealing machine which they can barely touch and that kills one of them per its hit among them,but all the primordial fears and terrors of the wolves breaking down your hovels and murdering everyone around you come into your head. Your sanity and sensibility is bound to take a hit. So yeah. Delirium works just as intended.<br /> <br /> Now if you really feel its overpowered and you're actually playing a Dark Ages game in Europe (i assume) you could easily say that all the reactions on the willpower chart are 2 higher, because the Ajaba are not part of the European cultural fears. I wouldn't in your place, because it's counterbalanced by the fact that someone will remember, the fact that the shifters enforce the Veil... and frankly, what do you think a Vampire with Presence does to an army?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T05:59:46-07:00","id":857650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Originally posted by <b>Innocent Flower </b>If the white howlers really wanted to, they could have driven rome out with a single pack and not needed to have risked their leaving their home unprotected. </div> </div> </div>Apart from the vampires, mages and other garou that had invested interest and a presence within the roman legions. Also bear in mind that this is the world of darkness so lets say a pack of howlers forced a legion to retreat/run away, what happens to every non legionnaire they encounter as they fall back. The fear caused and damage done would create a massive breeding ground for the wyrm.<br /> As for the werecreatures cleaning the earth, the war of rage means they are unlikely to ever unite with enough numbers to accomplish this and the similarity to the impergium would divide the garou and possible bring about a civil war. There is so much material published explaining how this is a bad idea, for any supernatural to attempt. That said it could make for one hell of a game just exploring one of these possibilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for delirium in mass combat, I tend to increase the willpower of regular people when they are in groups, people who are trained for and/or have seen combat may have higher than normal willpower. Private security drawn from military personnel are more likely to fall back in an organized fashion with suppressing fire, a street gang not so much. One roman legionnaire or man at arms vs a pack of werewolves, they will run, if they live that long, a hundred there will be panic sure but they will mostly fight, a thousand is a different story entirely.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day it is up to the ST to either use a bit of common sense and weigh up the numbers and experience of the enemies or go the other way and ramp up the absurdity because that can be fun once in a while as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11552-molono","name":"molono","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T13:24:37-07:00","id":857886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857611#post857611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing to keep in mind that a uniform group of soldiers is not likely to have the same random willpower as the populace. There is a certain kind of people who end up in the military and those people are usually not the high willpower people. High Willpower people are extraordinary, I mean, look at this.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Willpower measures a character\u2019s inner drive and ability to overcome unfavorable odds.<br /> \u2022 Spineless \u2022\u2022 Weak \u2022\u2022\u2022 Unassertive \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Diffident \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Certain \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022 Confident<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022 Determined \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022 Controlled \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Iron-willed \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Unshakable&quot;<br /> I feel like someone in the military is much more likely to have a high willpower rating based off the description than a normal person. So I feel like you'd have an even higher percentage in an army who would be able to resist it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11540-sausuna","name":"Sausuna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T13:34:11-07:00","id":857890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857611#post857611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a certain kind of people who end up in the military and those people are usually not the high willpower people.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Where the fuck do you get that idea? Honestly I'm damn near speechless that this bullshit made it past your brain through your fingers to your keyboard and onto your screen where your eyes then read it sent it back to your brain and you go &quot;Yea that sounds right&quot;<br /> <br /> Like seriously just taking the U.S. as an example only about 7.3% of the population has ever served in the military period. Just going off of that the would most likely be in the top 7-8% of the population.<br /> <br /> NOW generally speaking back in the middle ages this may or may not of been the case. Knights would of most certainly had a higher willpower as they we trained to fight and had done it most of their lives. Mercenary companies were probably similar to the knights. The peasant levies that had been drafted by their lords probably not as much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","name":"Seph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:43:23-07:00","id":857933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857611#post857611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a certain kind of people who end up in the military and those people are usually not the high willpower people.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">This is really pushing group attack territory. Please refrain from making blanket statements like this about the character of large groups of people.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857890#post857890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where the fuck do you get that idea? Honestly I'm damn near speechless that this bullshit made it past your brain through your fingers to your keyboard and onto your screen where your eyes then read it sent it back to your brain and you go &amp;quot;Yea that sounds right&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">This is absolutely not an appropriate response. I'm giving you a warning now, if you can't contribute to the discussion respectfully I will remove you from the thread.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T15:42:19-07:00","id":857969,"title":"","content":"Well, the Dark Ages book does explicitly say &quot;Werewolves who reveal themselves to a community of humans threaten all Garou, and they will be brought to a sept for judgment&quot; (p. 32). An army is certainly a &quot;community&quot; of sorts, so just enforce that. Even if it's not a werewolf proper, that doesn't mean there can't be consequences for reckless behavior. Enemies of Gaia might find a &quot;lone&quot; target a perfect mark for corruption, human superstition could make things harder for the group, and so on and so forth. The book even suggests a few problems that might immediately arise. You know what they say, with great power comes great responsibility. Sounds like a good roleplaying opportunity to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11549-chobin-hood","name":"Chobin Hood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11549_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:01:46-07:00","id":857975,"title":"","content":"Being objective as possible- The military would likely have a more wildly varying collection of willpower levels. On the one hand you might have the weak join the military because 'my parents did it' or 'it's the right thing to do' or 'I need to prove that I'm a man because everyone else doesn't think so' or 'civilian life is a struggle for me'. On the otherhand you've got people with genuine drive to prove they're the best or that they can aim for the top and make things around them greater. <br /> <br /> As for the training, It's either going to go way down or way up. Some are going to re-evaluate their things as worthless, others are going to see more worth in them. You can be the dehumanized jarhead or the empowered man. <br /> <br /> As redshirt as it sounds, a lot of soldiers will have the 'true love' merit. many of them will have a sense of responsibility to the man on their left (or, as above, a detachment from them because they've seen so much death) <br /> <br /> The werehyena wouldn't cause reduced delerium in places it's not native to. The unknown is still terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:08:18-07:00","id":857979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chobin Hood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857969#post857969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Dark Ages book does explicitly say &quot;Werewolves who reveal themselves to a community of humans threaten all Garou, and they will be brought to a sept for judgment&quot; (p. 32). An army is certainly a &quot;community&quot; of sorts, so just enforce that. Even if it's not a werewolf proper, that doesn't mean there can't be consequences for reckless behavior. Enemies of Gaia might find a &quot;lone&quot; target a perfect mark for corruption, human superstition could make things harder for the group, and so on and so forth. The book even suggests a few problems that might immediately arise. You know what they say, with great power comes great responsibility. Sounds like a good roleplaying opportunity to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Playing off of this, is this going on in Europe? Because if so this would be a Fera exposing himself in a land of wolves where the War of VERY supported and only died down due to the other shifters dying or disappearing. Even if Europeans misidentify a raging Fera...it doesnt mean Garou won't look into it and find that its not even a wolf. Imagine a metis hyena to Dark Ages Garou, everything strange about it, and the myths that the other shifters support the wyrm. Now they find one traveling with vampries? A mortal army can quickly become the least of this PC's problems and full plots can grow from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 04-02-2016, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:12:38-07:00","id":857981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857979#post857979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Playing off of this, is this going on in Europe? Because if so this would be a Fera exposing himself in a land of wolves where the War of VERY supported and only died down due to the other shifters dying or disappearing. Even if Europeans misidentify a raging Fera...it doesnt mean Garou won't look into it and find that its not even a wolf. Imagine a metis hyena to Dark Ages Garou, everything strange about it, and the myths that the other shifters support the wyrm. Now they find one traveling with vampries? A mortal army can quickly become the least of this PC's problems and full plots can grow from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The op said its a dark ages vampire game that he's letting a player use a shifter as a concession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:16:40-07:00","id":857985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857981#post857981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The op said its a dark ages vampire game that he's letting a player use a shifter as a concession.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok...doesn't change the fact that werewolves in Europe wouldn't be a realistic problem......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:18:32-07:00","id":857986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857933#post857933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:red\">This is absolutely not an appropriate response. I'm giving you a warning now, if you can't contribute to the discussion respectfully I will remove you from the thread.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize, I lost my frenzy roll <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857975#post857975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being objective as possible- The military would likely have a more wildly varying collection of willpower levels. On the one hand you might have the weak join the military because 'my parents did it' or 'it's the right thing to do' or 'I need to prove that I'm a man because everyone else doesn't think so' or 'civilian life is a struggle for me'. On the otherhand you've got people with genuine drive to prove they're the best or that they can aim for the top and make things around them greater.<br /> <br /> As for the training, It's either going to go way down or way up. Some are going to re-evaluate their things as worthless, others are going to see more worth in them. You can be the dehumanized jarhead or the empowered man.<br /> <br /> As redshirt as it sounds, a lot of soldiers will have the 'true love' merit. many of them will have a sense of responsibility to the man on their left (or, as above, a detachment from them because they've seen so much death)<br /> <br /> The werehyena wouldn't cause reduced delerium in places it's not native to. The unknown is still terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes the military would have varying degrees of Willpower. However Willpower is stated as :<br /> <span style=\"color:#672625\"><span style=\"font-family:Averoigne-Regular\">W<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">illpower measures a character\u2019s inner drive and ability to overcome unfavorable odds. It has a permanent rating and<br /> a temporary pool of points.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> From the book so regardless of their reason for joining the military they would have to have a high inner drive to make it through. Yes there will be differences just like not every baker is super creative, or not every write the next Edgar Allen Poe. But the average WP of someone in the military would be higher than the average WP of the general populace due to the type of people that typically join and the concentration of said people.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","name":"Seph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:21:34-07:00","id":857990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857985#post857985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok...doesn't change the fact that werewolves in Europe wouldn't be a realistic problem......</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if he doesn't want to bother with that aspect of the game. If I was at the table, I would be pretty upset if the plot got derailed because snowflake decided to drag the rest of the game into werewolf nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:26:19-07:00","id":857993,"title":"","content":"I threw it out as a possibility not as a &quot;THIS MUST HAPPEN&quot;. It was intended to be food for thought. Its a realistic draw back to being so unique in a game. Personally if I wanted to run a vampire game, I'd just tell them upfront its going to be vampires, nothing else. I've had possible players turn out to not play my games because they wanted to be something that wasn't meshing with what I wanted to run (Shih from Demon Hunter X, vampire, demon).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:59:27-07:00","id":858012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857990#post857990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt; snowflake<br /> &gt; werewolf nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice to know Vampire is the only sensible, not-snowflake character type in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11549-chobin-hood","name":"Chobin Hood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11549_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:04:39-07:00","id":858014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chobin Hood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=858012#post858012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice to know Vampire is the only sensible, not-snowflake character type in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Way to take what I said out of context, bravo. I would feel the same way if it was a werewolf game and the person who just had to play a vampire dragged the game to an Elysium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:46:39-07:00","id":858035,"title":"","content":"You should only be using an ajaba if you're in africa, and africa is fine for the dark ages. If you're using him in europe.... super mega low profile. <br /> <br /> You don't drag him into garou politics. The most the ajaba gets from that is a pack trying to kill him, not just for being fera, but also for consorting with vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:48:20-07:00","id":858036,"title":"","content":"For the record, we really enjoy our werehyena. She's a great player and writer (it's a forum based game). We also have no problem with her splat choice. I myself started this thread because I was unfamiliar with Delirium and we have a major battle coming up and I thought what I mentioned in the op could easily happen.<br /> <br /> As a testament to how great of a player our werehyena is she already had as very simple work around planned that will work very well IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","user":"Seph","date":". 04-02-2016, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","name":"Seph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:53:38-07:00","id":858042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=857986#post857986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the book so regardless of their reason for joining the military they would have to have a high inner drive to make it through. Yes there will be differences just like not every baker is super creative, or not every write the next Edgar Allen Poe. But the average WP of someone in the military would be higher than the average WP of the general populace due to the type of people that typically join and the concentration of said people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went from the average WP of a levy man. Today's proffesional soldiers have very little to do with the traditional &quot;toss bodies at a target until everyone stops challenging your claim it was yours all along&quot;. Sadly, after the fall of the Roman Legions, the level of proffesionalism, training and investment into troops has been downright horrible for centuries afterwards. There were highly trained special units with better gear and more hands on experience, but most levied men would be used as a small cog in the meatgrinder.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if you felt offended by the comment, it was meant for a whole different type of soldiers which would represent most armies in the Dark Ages. I would expect that most commoners with high willpower forced to join up would look for ways to get out of it - as many colorful folk tales seem to regale (check out brothers Grimm for instance)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:59:05-07:00","id":858047,"title":"","content":"Would also like to remind everyone of the number 1 rule in an RPG, have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","name":"Seph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T18:02:41-07:00","id":858048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=858036#post858036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, we really enjoy our werehyena. She's a great player and writer (it's a forum based game). We also have no problem with her splat choice. I myself started this thread because I was unfamiliar with Delirium and we have a major battle coming up and I thought what I mentioned in the op could easily happen.<br /> <br /> As a testament to how great of a player our werehyena is she already had as very simple work around planned that will work very well IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can like her and still have her hunted by Garou. I was seeing it as a plot since she's consorting with vampires, avoiding them/pulling in kindred support would be something she could use to survive. Garou however are a huge reason for her to want to maintain a low profile and avoid those situations (which you said she did anyway). <br /> <br /> While I wouldn't be really down with something like this in my games, it doesn't mean others aren't. When I made my comment about not allowing things in my games, its more a statement on my style and not &quot;you're doing it wrong&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T07:53:47-07:00","id":858341,"title":"","content":"Levy moral is typically poor when looking at a Dark Ages army, these are essentially farmers and lower tradesmen forced to take up arms with little to no training beyond the very basics (this is why they use spears). Professional soldiers (including knights) are far rarer and will typically hold to a higher WP standard and then you have things like the Crusading Orders which will have as an average a higher WP and probably True Faith too. <br /> <br /> Lots of armies spent lots of time running away.<br /> <br /> However, it would be reasonable to boost the &quot;effective&quot; WP of mortals involved if they are in a situation with something to fight FOR. Defending home or family can boost resolve to face terrors. Also it's a perfect situation to use the Leadership ability, for the leader of these forces to strengthen their soldiers Will and Resolve to face down the bloody horrors of battle (especially vs monsters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T05:04:04-07:00","id":858898,"title":"","content":"I'd agree that in a field battle not every fighter would be able to see and realize the presence of the Crinos, and therefore not be immediately affected by Delirium. That is until directly faced with the beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:17:27-07:00","id":860523,"title":"","content":"&quot;Players accustomed to gutting whomever they like and letting the Veil cover their tracks and in for a rude surprise in a <b>Werewolf: The Dark Ages </b>game. The Delerium is <i>not</i> that strong in medieval times...&quot;<br /> &quot;...However, results that indicate disbelief should be substituted for beserk rage...&quot;<br /> Werewolf: The Dark Ages, p. 20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:47:36-07:00","id":860541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=860523#post860523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Players accustomed to gutting whomever they like and letting the Veil cover their tracks and in for a rude surprise in a <b>Werewolf: The Dark Ages </b>game. The Delerium is <i>not</i> that strong in medieval times...&quot;<br /> &quot;...However, results that indicate disbelief should be substituted for beserk rage...&quot;<br /> Werewolf: The Dark Ages, p. 20.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm puzzled as to how that's actually possible, given the time table of when the Impergium occurred and when it ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:07:46-07:00","id":860571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=860541#post860541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm puzzled as to how that's actually possible, given the time table of when the Impergium occurred and when it ended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf and editing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T17:22:12-07:00","id":860658,"title":"","content":"I think it more garou and ancestors being unreliable. (or, well, garou don't ask too much of their ancestors about it) <br /> <br /> I think, probably, that the delirium is based on what level of the gauntlet (or similar item. The changeling one seems most appropriate) you're used to living under. Which is why many native tribes don't suffer it, but loose that ability when they start communicating with the weaver-people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T04:13:46-07:00","id":860933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=860571#post860571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf and editing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Since some people are less affected than others, this might be true for the average person in Dark Ages. I mean, people weren't as rational as they are today (a prejudiced moder person might argue), therefore their rational mind is less developed and less likely to shut down, when the unexplained happens - a lot of things are unexplained...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T17:48:25-07:00","id":861463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think it more garou and ancestors being unreliable. (or, well, garou don't ask too much of their ancestors about it) </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think, probably, that the delirium is based on what level of the gauntlet (or similar item. The changeling one seems most appropriate) you're used to living under. Which is why many native tribes don't suffer it, but loose that ability when they start communicating with the weaver-people.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Only if you're playing Mage. Werewolf assumes that the Garou fucked up by openly brutalizing humans for a few tens of thousands of years. And before that, the Mokole bungled things twice, through the Dragon Wars that wrecked Mnesis from the Wonder Works that it used to make possible, and then again through helping to apply certain selection pressures on various primates to make them more like the Kings.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=860933#post860933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since some people are less affected than others, this might be true for the average person in Dark Ages. I mean, people weren't as rational as they are today (a prejudiced moder person might argue), therefore their rational mind is less developed and less likely to shut down, when the unexplained happens - a lot of things are unexplained...</div> </div> </div> </div>That explanation is extremely bad. All the genes we have for our brain development were in place a long, long time before the dark ages of Europe. Besides, if you think that modern people are necessarily rational at all, much less more so by some strange metric, I'm not even sure where to begin addressing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T01:10:07-07:00","id":861677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=861463#post861463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That explanation is extremely bad. All the genes we have for our brain development were in place a long, long time before the dark ages of Europe. Besides, if you think that modern people are necessarily rational at all, much less more so by some strange metric, I'm not even sure where to begin addressing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you arguing that the people in the Dark Ages on average probably had a world view that could incorporate a raging werewolf more easily than a modern day human?<br /> <br /> If not, than there is really not a reason, why such people should be less affected by the sight of such a being and after the fact would retain their mental health while retaining a vague recollection of the event, as opposed to completely blocking it out.<br /> <br /> And, we are talking the WoD here. It is quite possible that humans didn't have genes in the dark ages what so ever. Mendel didn't discover discrete inheritable units in plants until 1864. And without the existence of genes being part of Consensus it probably wasn't part of Reality either.<br /> Also, we are talking of a world where magick and hedge magic are real, and more openly practised. The Dictum Mortuum isn't fully in effect and it is still the age of Sundering, when the banality is only starting to form and the Mists are only starting to separate fae and man.<br /> <br /> I find it in no way hard to believe that people confronted with this reality have not that hard a time to cope with the sight of a werewolf than modern era people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T02:15:51-07:00","id":861696,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with DIno here. Delirium is provoked by primal fears of horrible things murdering you in the night, and the trauma of watching everyone but you dying around you getting imprinted in your &quot;genetics&quot;. This is not lessened by being more superstitious, or heightened by being too rational. It's a primordial terror and it has always been the same. Heck, one could more easily argue that it would lessen over time, rather then be weaker 1500 years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T03:09:08-07:00","id":861718,"title":"","content":"Well, we had that discussion in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/845544-delerium-and-rationality-or-logic\">Delerium and Rationality or Logic...</a>-Topic.<br /> <br /> And, in the source material, the Delirium has been tied to both, fear (due to the Impergium) and rationality.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:33:13-07:00","id":862153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=861677#post861677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you arguing that the people in the Dark Ages on average probably had a world view that could incorporate a raging werewolf more easily than a modern day human?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Both are equally likely to collapse in a denial-driven psychological shutoff valve. It's like something from Lovecraft, only with a critter that is comparatively much more sedate and closer to reality than shoggoths and the like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If not, than there is really not a reason, why such people should be less affected by the sight of such a being and after the fact would retain their mental health while retaining a vague recollection of the event, as opposed to completely blocking it out. </div> </div> </div>Willpower. Higher SAN rating to start with. That kind of thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, we are talking the WoD here. It is quite possible that humans didn't have genes in the dark ages </div> </div> </div>You're in the wrong forum for that take, and you know it. Consensus is only for Mage; Werewolf assumes that latter day discoveries of science have always been the case and that they won't suddenly change. The Earth is billions of years old, the stars are older, matter is arranged into atoms and molecules, and inheritance is molecular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I find it in no way hard to believe that people confronted with this reality have not that hard a time to cope with the sight of a werewolf than modern era people. </div> </div> </div>They just use a different rationalization, not a &quot;lesser&quot; one. Whatever era, humans who survive the attack fit it into whatever innocuous part of life with which they're familiar and nervously go back to what they were doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T02:08:55-07:00","id":863534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=862153#post862153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're in the wrong forum for that take, and you know it. Consensus is only for Mage; Werewolf assumes that latter day discoveries of science have always been the case and that they won't suddenly change. The Earth is billions of years old, the stars are older, matter is arranged into atoms and molecules, and inheritance is molecular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf clearly states that the worlds were once one. Werewolf also states, that inheritance is spiritual (at least in the sense of pure breed, being a garou, possibly in the sense of being kin, and by extension immunity to Delirium).<br /> So, sure, conesnsus is a Mage principle, but that Werewolf assumes that the world has always been the way modern science does is a bit fat fetched. I mean, there is a high civilisation of dinosaurs in werewolf canon - as well as a paradise like state, that today is reflected in the Summer Country Umbra realm. A state of existence that maybe didn't knew death, yet. How does that fit with a scientific world?<br /> <br /> In the end, I really don't have stakes in it, if one thinks humans from the Dark Ages could or could not be more resistant to the Delirium or not. I remember that some ethnic groups in modern times could be to some degree resistant if they weren't influenced by western upbringing. One could make an argument, that people from the DA would also have not been influenced by western upbringing, yet.<br /> <br /> I don't have the books to read the Delirium entries in the DA Werewolf books, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:36:49-07:00","id":863630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=863534#post863534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf clearly states that the worlds were once one. Werewolf also states, that inheritance is spiritual (at least in the sense of pure breed, being a garou, possibly in the sense of being kin, and by extension immunity to Delirium).<br /> So, sure, conesnsus is a Mage principle, but that Werewolf assumes that the world has always been the way modern science does is a bit fat fetched.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's close enough. While I do take issue with elements of Shattered Dreams*, its time periods fit in snugly with the outline of deep time provided courtesy of geology and fossil evidence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*I don't like time travel, and don't think that Chiyou should have been described as a Garou like in Blood and Silk.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, there is a high civilisation of dinosaurs in werewolf canon - as well as a paradise like state, that today is reflected in the Summer Country Umbra realm. A state of existence that maybe didn't knew death, yet. How does that fit with a scientific world? </div> </div> </div>The Kings and their Mokole relatives fucked up pretty hard and blew themselves up with spiritual weapons that ended up having a failure of existence when they broke, to such an extent that the possibilities they represented vacated reality altogether. Umbral Realms, meanwhile, are parts of the spirit, and are so distant from the physical world that their influence is considerably less than what you get by going around changing things in the Penumbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the end, I really don't have stakes in it, if one thinks humans from the Dark Ages could or could not be more resistant to the Delirium or not. I remember that some ethnic groups in modern times could be to some degree resistant if they weren't influenced by western upbringing. One could make an argument, that people from the DA would also have not been influenced by western upbringing, yet.<br /> <br /> I don't have the books to read the Delirium entries in the DA Werewolf books, though. </div> </div> </div>The entries on it aren't as important as the metatextual reasons that it is in the game, and those boil down to &quot;the Garou fucked up by terrorizing humans for such a long time that humans became utterly terrified of the Garou and can't cope with their existence.&quot; We just went over this a few posts up, along with the Mokole having flamingo-ed up in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:03:51-07:00","id":863654,"title":"","content":"As I pointed out, I don't like the &quot;Garou terrorized mankind&quot;-statement, because it makes no sense and wasn't there in 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> In any case it is spiritual in nature, for homid garou and human kinfolk are biologically indistinguishable from humans, yet, they aren't affected by Delirium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:21:33-07:00","id":863702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=863654#post863654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I pointed out, I don't like the &quot;Garou terrorized mankind&quot;-statement, because it makes no sense and wasn't there in 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> In any case it is spiritual in nature, for homid garou and human kinfolk are biologically indistinguishable from humans, yet, they aren't affected by Delirium.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Impergium and the Decimation of man is in 2nd edition, and Decimating a whole species would pretty much qualify as utter, abject terror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:57:34-07:00","id":863729,"title":"","content":"There is a distinct difference, on how it is presented. I got into detail about this, in another topic.<br /> <br /> But, basically, there is a difference in how the Impergium is presented. In a time, when humans lived in small settlements it makes a difference to state &quot;The garou regularly came to the villages and culled the human population.&quot; or to state &quot;They terrorized the humans.&quot;<br /> <br /> Culling has a distinct meaning, to kill the weak/old/sick to protect the herd. I can see, why garou would do such a thing, and I can see why the humans developed a fear for the garou.<br /> <br /> Terrorizing is a different behaviour. It implies 'fear mongering', but revised doesn't give any reason for such a behaviour, except that garou were megalomantic douchbags, living out their superiority complex on the humans. But I find it doesn't make sense, that garou were that way, and it makes even less sense, tat the garou of today, who should glorify their ancestors to some degree, would tell each other such things.<br /> <br /> So, the supposed behaviour on the garou's side, that leads to the Delirium in humans, is an action, that doesn't make sense in the first place. Besides that, 2nd Edition also states, that humans rational mind is partly responsible for the Delirium, not just the Impergium and a supposed inherited super-fear-reaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T10:12:00-07:00","id":863745,"title":"","content":"The Impergium dates from the very first Werewolf book. Page 14 of the 1E Core Book, to be precise. It's even stated that the Impergium's trauma drove the entire human species mad from three thousand years of 'culling'. It has been a consistent element from the get-go: Werewolves came, killed the shit out of humans, and that drove mankind batshit insane. The culling was not in the sense you mean: it was in the same way we cull wolves or deer or emus or kangaroos or hell, for a great example, feral cats. We don't just kill the weak/old/sick 'to protect the herd'. We brutally slaughter any and every one of them we see until their population is reduced to a level we deem acceptable. And just like our actions, the Garou's actions had unintended consequences.<br /> <br /> I don't understand your objection to a fundamental element of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T13:40:13-07:00","id":863872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=863745#post863745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Impergium dates from the very first Werewolf book. Page 14 of the 1E Core Book, to be precise. It's even stated that the Impergium's trauma drove the entire human species mad from three thousand years of 'culling'. It has been a consistent element from the get-go: Werewolves came, killed the shit out of humans, and that drove mankind batshit insane. The culling was not in the sense you mean: it was in the same way we cull wolves or deer or emus or kangaroos or hell, for a great example, feral cats. We don't just kill the weak/old/sick 'to protect the herd'. We brutally slaughter any and every one of them we see until their population is reduced to a level we deem acceptable. And just like our actions, the Garou's actions had unintended consequences.<br /> <br /> I don't understand your objection to a fundamental element of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Additionally, the only change in later editions was to dramatically increase the time period over which it occurred, with Revised starting to move toward a less settled number, as we have in W20, which basically boils down to &quot;lots of thousands of years, starting not long after modern humans came into being and ending only a few generations before Catalhuyuk and various other recognized cities.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T09:44:02-07:00","id":865981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=858036#post858036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, we really enjoy our werehyena. She's a great player and writer (it's a forum based game). We also have no problem with her splat choice. I myself started this thread because I was unfamiliar with Delirium and we have a major battle coming up and I thought what I mentioned in the op could easily happen.<br /> <br /> As a testament to how great of a player our werehyena is she already had as very simple work around planned that will work very well IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I am the only one, but I'd love to hear the very simple workaround! :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:59:01-07:00","id":867134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=865981#post865981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I am the only one, but I'd love to hear the very simple workaround! :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. Our player grabbed a merit (or maybe two) that basically made Hispo/Cronac (Giant bear sized Hyena) her most viable combat form which doesn't cause Delerium, so there's no reason to use Crinos when an Army is bearing down on us when Hispo is stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","name":"Seph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:22:20-07:00","id":867143,"title":"","content":"Uh. Hispo causes Delirium, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:47:38-07:00","id":867166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=867143#post867143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh. Hispo causes Delirium, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ajaba Hispo/Crocas doesn't cause Delerium look it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","user":"Seph","date":". 04-17-2016, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","name":"Seph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:56:05-07:00","id":867177,"title":"","content":"Double post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","name":"Seph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T01:20:29-07:00","id":867433,"title":"","content":"One Houserule, we occasionally employ on our table, is that the collective Willpower of a group rises, once said group has grown to a certain size.<br /> You know, pack mentality.<br /> We setteld on every increment of 10. So in a group of 10+ People, everybodys Willpower would be considerd 1 point higher, that what it usually is for purposes like delirium.<br /> In a Group of 100+ People it would be 2 points higher, in a Group of 1.000+ People 3 points higher, 10.000+ people 4 points higher etc.<br /> <br /> In that scenario, an &quot;army&quot; attacking some crinos garou would have quite a few soldiers who flee in panic, but the bulk of them would grid their teeth and press on.<br /> <br /> Sidenote:<br /> This also works out, if you play a different game-line, like mage or changeling. This way it gets quite a lot harder to mind-controll half of the city in one big ritual or something among these lines.<br /> When playing changeling, we usually raise the collective banality in the same way, and it works very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6112,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","user":"Seki","date":". 04-18-2016, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T22:12:09-07:00","id":875286,"title":"","content":"In the past, for large groups i have allowed leaders to make a check on their leadership/instruction talents to try and bolster their men's willpower, even just temporarily. Cha+leadership Diff 8. Each success they get, adds 1 to everyone under their command's Willpower RATING (not gives actual points though) for things such as Delerium resisting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T01:16:18-07:00","id":875422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=875286#post875286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the past, for large groups i have allowed leaders to make a check on their leadership/instruction talents to try and bolster their men's willpower, even just temporarily. Cha+leadership Diff 8. Each success they get, adds 1 to everyone under their command's Willpower RATING (not gives actual points though) for things such as Delerium resisting...</div> </div> </div> </div>How does high leadership affect the fact that your brain literally tries to shut down and NOPE! the fact that it has seen something so fundamentally horrible as to be ingrained in human racial memory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T01:27:50-07:00","id":875427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=875422#post875422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does high leadership affect the fact that your brain literally tries to shut down and NOPE! the fact that it has seen something so fundamentally horrible as to be ingrained in human racial memory?</div> </div> </div> </div>How can leadership affect anyone to do stupid things, up to but not limited by, committing suicide?<br /> <br /> Also the brain doesn't shut down in the delirium. Only some people get catatonic, others try to flee or even attack, so the brain (while not making rational decisions) still processes outside input and controls motor function. It ain't that big of a leap to believe, that in such a state a person might be rather susceptible to a person who tells him to either flee or attack...<br /> I mean, it's not that there is a rational thought telling him &quot;this doesn't make sense&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T02:53:20-07:00","id":875447,"title":"","content":"... read that delirium chart and tell me again that orders would matter to anyone below Willpower 6-7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T12:32:15-07:00","id":875853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=875422#post875422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does high leadership affect the fact that your brain literally tries to shut down and NOPE! the fact that it has seen something so fundamentally horrible as to be ingrained in human racial memory?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever watch war films where leaders give 'resounding battle speeches before hand&quot;? its a similar thing. Bolster their morale??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:09:38-07:00","id":876032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=875853#post875853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ever watch war films where leaders give 'resounding battle speeches before hand&quot;? its a similar thing. Bolster their morale??</div> </div> </div> </div>It's difficult to imagine, because war is horrendous, but the Delirium is supposed to be worse. Also, the difficulty on that is going to be a bit higher, since Wits + Occult allows resistance at difficulty 9, and experiences with terrifying werewolves is Occult's bag. Leadership, not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T18:24:50-07:00","id":876154,"title":"","content":"Would you be more ok with it, if i say raised it to 9 (or even 10)??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T18:44:56-07:00","id":876174,"title":"","content":"Since we are on the subject of great military speeches I'll paraphrase Patton &quot;cause when reach over and put your hand into the pile of goo that was your best friends face, you will know what to do.&quot; <br /> <br /> I'm pretty so no speech ever would rally some peasants armed with sticks when a 9 foot tall wolf monster tears their commander in half and chuckles when it's pointy stick wounds heal in rapid fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T20:51:17-07:00","id":876234,"title":"","content":"It would not be unreasonable to give a temporary buff to move them from the 'break and run' to 'scream and try and murder everything you see' for a solid leadership roll, especially if they've had prior experience with garou or been psychologically prepared (as far as one can be) for exposure. Anything more is probably right out. The guy who was still going to collapse and curl up in a ball and wait to die is still going to. The guy going to blindly flee no matter what is still going to. But the guy able to stay a little bit aware while he runs or rational enough to try and bargain his way out with the Garou, he might be able to turn around and fight so long as the line holds and their commander is still alive, active, and fighting with them. Essentially, to make 5 or 6 Willpower to act - for a scene - as if they had 7. 4 is still going to be blindly aggressive towards the threat, 3 and below are still going to wait to die or break and run no matter what. But those two fringe cases might be able to fight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T01:07:21-07:00","id":876342,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Hence my temp boost for what their rating is (for that delerium chart) for a great leadership+cha roll..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T08:14:23-07:00","id":876650,"title":"","content":"I just don't see it. Delirium is a sanity shattering effect. I don't see Erwin Rommel being much better at preventing this then John Q Public. Maybe a max of +1, but we're talking about a situation where someone with stupidly high leadership could literally have whole units fighting effectively against Garou. If this was a thing in setting it would surely be corroborated by Project Twilight and the First Teams... yet all they speak off is exposure experience (high occult) and wacky drugs that make you not give a fuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T14:32:22-07:00","id":876980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=876650#post876650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't see it. Delirium is a sanity shattering effect. I don't see Erwin Rommel being much better at preventing this then John Q Public. Maybe a max of +1, but we're talking about a situation where someone with stupidly high leadership could literally have whole units fighting effectively against Garou. If this was a thing in setting it would surely be corroborated by Project Twilight and the First Teams... yet all they speak off is exposure experience (high occult) and wacky drugs that make you not give a fuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>And also cause some forms of brain damage. So, I guess, order people to hit themselves in certain parts of the head before the engagement, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T18:59:32-07:00","id":877223,"title":"","content":"Something i'm wondering about this army question, we've determined that in a delirium situation most or at least a large part of the army will flee or curl up int a ball sobbing, how would you all handle an army lead by some vampiric master or their ghouls with dominate or prescense?<br /> <br /> I think prescense effects would probably just work like the bonus given for good leadership like above, but how would you handle it if parts or a ,ways less likely, the entire army was conditioned by dominate to fight exactly as their leader commanded them. a diffucult army to make but maybe not impossible. <br /> <br /> How do you think armies like those would hold?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T21:05:52-07:00","id":877295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857414-werewolf-delirium-vs-army?p=876650#post876650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't see it. Delirium is a sanity shattering effect. I don't see Erwin Rommel being much better at preventing this then John Q Public. Maybe a max of +1, but we're talking about a situation where someone with stupidly high leadership could literally have whole units fighting effectively against Garou. If this was a thing in setting it would surely be corroborated by Project Twilight and the First Teams... yet all they speak off is exposure experience (high occult) and wacky drugs that make you not give a fuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a sanity shattering effect yes - but the key point you're not grasping is that at the willpower levels I'm talking about, the characteristic of the experience is still one of rationality. At willpower 5 and 6, the response is to flee to safety and to bargain respectively. That flight is controlled and rational - locking doors, using a car - rather than blindly running screaming into the night. At these two points, the response becomes characterized by an ability to think - and if the ability to think remains, it is not unreasonable that an especially able leader might be able to pull them back to fighting. 63% of humanity will still lie down and wait to die, go berserk, or run blindly into the night. This proposal makes just makes another 23% <i>potentially</i> able to stand and fight if properly lead and trained. Note that I don't mean 'to be calm and cool under pressure'. We're talking the kind of screaming, bullet-spraying, badly coordinated, screaming prayers-to-god fighting we've seen a lot of out of the Middle East lately.<br /> <br /> Notably, the willpower directly below these 2 strata demands an outright and immediate violent response - to stand and fight. The big difference is that response isn't a rational one so they won't reload or work together. The proposal is essentially to actually downgrade the response to a more primitive one, while retaining some of the ability to think that characterizes 5-and-up willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T21:19:05-07:00","id":877305,"title":"","content":"And even with a roll, it doesn't mean that success is going to come. Even at my (diff 9) where i had it, there were still times i had PCs (and even NPCS) fail that roll. Heck one PC (who had hired a 20 man merc group to go a BSD hunting for a Kinfolk focused game) botched his leadership+cha roll.. so i said HE was now affected by the same result his troops were (they had 3 will by the way)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:14:11-07:00","id":884940,"title":"","content":"#Guys, did you ever stand on a medival battlefield, someone left, someone right and two behind? in tight formation, you can't go anywhere but forward. Tight formation is the usual formation for pikes, helebards, archery weapons and the antic phalanx. All those happen to be the arms used by large troops and militia. So let's assume a tight packed militia of 200 people: 20 wide, 10 deep.<br /> <br /> Let's look at the chart again: who of those is actually going not to fight? the WP1 and WP2 clearly, WP3 tries to retreat and reason it away - which in a big battle would mean go back to the back lines - but they are pushed forward from behind, they have to fight. WP4, Berserk, stroms in. WP5 retreats as orderly as it can - but still is pushed forward instead, so has to fight. WP6 will plead and bargain and try not to get hurt, so let's call those out again. 7+ is fight at will, so all in. That makes... 10%+20%+10%=40% of people that will not be able to fight and which don't fight when pressed to do so because of circumstances. Also, only the first two lines can see anything but backs, the rest can't see, so can't get delirium. If the outermost are the standfast (which was the usual tactic: put the vets at the edges to ensure the flanks do't fall), then the whole formation might stand because the central ones are forced to fight because they can not go anywhere but for those 40% that will not be able to because they are catatonic, deny to harm or fleeing without even a tiny bit of reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T03:36:23-07:00","id":886080,"title":"","content":"Since the subject is the Dark Ages, the phalanx is not really an option, and once the melee is started, very little of the formations will survive. Add to that the fact that the lines will very shortly stay as they should be, since the Garou would run straight in and multipaly the Delirium effect once he's inside slaughtering shit.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I have no idea why Garou would bother fighting in a stand up fight like this. It's inefficient, breaks the Veil, and you're so much better at murdering the army during the night, since they will not be prepared, considering that combat was not conducted at night. Be Vlad the Impaler, not William Wallace!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T15:25:46-07:00","id":886673,"title":"","content":"That too... but the middleage kew the anti-knight formation from pikemen - the tight packed Pike square, one next to the other. It is even tighter than the Phalanx, and relies on badass soldiers, that brace for impact against riders on horses which weigh about a ton together. With that kind of possible deadly tactic for the pike square, I estimate them to stand (high WP). But on the other hand: in an open battle, I would field 3 troup types: archers to rain death from aboce, pikemen to shield them, and very light or unarmored cavalry as skirmishers - which are badass troups too, as they tend to die quickly and thus are expected to have more WP. Why these? action economy!<br /> <br /> You got 1 defense without splitting actions or spending rage.<br /> <br /> Archers just ignore the whole delirium for distance - and dodging arrows is near impossible, especially dodging like 40 or 50 well enough aimed arrows from a 20x5 archer line. While they don't do that much damage each (and some is soaked), the sheer number of them will most likely accumulate 1 lethal suware after another, till the deadly 7 are there, and then add up more till not even 'staying active' emergency regen can heal that much overflow damage.<br /> <br /> The higher WP Pikemen do a brace action - which results in the wolf gaining damage from getting in fast - and they are in a formation that would allow at least 2 rows deep to attack if they stand - so possibly 8 to 10 attacks. Let's assume the pikemen have average 3/3 and have to roll a 7... without WP, each attack can expect 3,1% botch, 16,96% Fail; Succeses: 21,42% 1 Success, 24,98% 2 successes etc. Now, If the wolf just charges in, he can kill one of them, then gets 7to 9 attacks, that most likely hit, having some chance to do damage, better if they use silver tipped pikes. They even might use the brace maneuver, doing even more damage. The wolf might not survive the second round because of action economy. If he gets in slow to avoid getting braced, they even get one more attack but loose the brace damage bonus and he can possibly dodge one or two - but in the time he needs to get close enough to get to claw distance, he receives at least one, possibly two rounds of attacks - which might kill the werewolf - the sheer ammount of attacks and damage to soak ensures that some of the soak rolls do at least 1 square of damage, which sums up till overflow - and an impaled werewolf.<br /> <br /> Last, light armored skirmishers. They come from the side, ride by, and do slashes. While the Wolf could brace and kill one of them, the others get a free slash at the wolf. Which means, he has to soak about... how many horsemen fit into a line of 60 yards? 20? 20 attacks at the strength of the horse with the speed bonus damage... Maybe 3 out of 10 hit, that's 6 attacks with something like... I estimate 10 damage dice - which is pretty much like an average of 5 damage, and 4-6 Damage with 65% of all the rolls. With 5 soak dice, in 70% of the rolls 1-4 damage get past (best chance 2-3). With 6 soak dice, it is 65% on that margin (best chance: 2). Even with astonishing 10 soak dice, in 55% of the rolls 1-4 damage are scored (1 is the best chance - 18.5%)! With 6 riders managing that attac, and those average damages... I guess 20 light cavalry will gutt a werewolf in a ride by as long as they are battlehardy enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, action economy by battlehardy veterans is a kill for the vets. But how to make these? Make them supernatural by any means - ghouling suffices! And with an army, you spend each soldier 1 Blood, then gain 1 from his veins to feed the next. As a result you have an army ignoring delirium. Or you use dominate - you can push them that way. Or you use Presence to boost the WP. Or you add a priest to the regiment - one with True Faith. That might negate Delirium. Or you take an army that is made up by people with true faith and call it a crusade! True faith 1 is not so uncommon in the dark ages. Or you go the evil way, turning the army into very very weak fomori without any extrapowers. Or a mage makes them technically constructs by altering them a very tiny bit - and thus making them supernatural and immune to delirium. really, ANYTHING that makes them supernatural makes me bet onto the army for action economy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:23:28-07:00","id":886727,"title":"","content":"Rage recovery does not, by default, consider overflow damage. Everything is considered to end at Incapacitated, and even one success will make you active again, albeit a -5, and send you into a berserk frenzy.<br /> <br /> Also, the tribe most likely to go out of its way to directly strike down an army like that has a number of Gifts to make them surprisingly effective against it, like Scream of Gaia, the howl Gifts (one of which, if performed in unison by an entire pack, will make it nearly impossible for the pike line to stand its ground, and another of which allows them to inflict lethal damage against any one target that they can see, at no cost, and one that makes everyone feel disastrously hungry, to the tune of losing two dice from all rolls), Shadow of the Impergium (your Willpower is now 5 points lower to determine how you'll react!), and Terror of the Dire Wolf (anything even remotely human other than Garou and Fera, or which was formerly human, now suffers the Delirium). There really is no CC among the Garou like Red Talon or Wendigo CC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.t